{"metadata":{"description":"Content-addressed audit indexes across independent DeepSeek Harness evidence producers","id":"gh:1333853983","install_available":true,"language":"JavaScript","name":"dsh-audit-bundle","slug":"dongsheng123132/dsh-audit-bundle","topics":["ai-agent","audit","deepseek-harness","dsh","dsh-plugin","evidence","mcp","merkle"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Content-addressed audit indexes across independent DeepSeek Harness evidence producers"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dsh-audit-bundle"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"**Maintainer / Author：He Fangsheng (贺方升 / 贺去病; also known as Dosen) · hequbing.com**"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"Content-addressed audit indexes across independent DeepSeek Harness evidence producers."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"Version 0.2 adds a formal proof-only Codex MCP surface, host-neutral DSH ToolDefinitions, real ToolR"},{"id":"p5s2","text":"untime calls and a stock Web Loader regression test. The package exposes namespace exports only and "},{"id":"p5s3","text":"does not bundle a second DSH runtime."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"This plugin is not an SBOM scanner, signer, audit logger, policy engine or archive. Existing tools a"},{"id":"p6s2","text":"lready scan dependencies and individual 2Origin plugins already produce release, runtime, recovery, "},{"id":"p6s3","text":"lineage and policy evidence. The missing layer is a small verifier that proves a particular subject/"},{"id":"p6s4","text":"revision has enough pinned evidence from allowed, independent producers to cover declared controls."},{"id":"p7s1","text":"## Contract"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"An explicit manifest declares:"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"- one subject ID and revision;
- required controls with minimum eligible evidence, minimum distinct "},{"id":"p9s2","text":"producers and allowed evidence types;
- evidence files pinned by SHA-256;
- JSON Pointers that bind "},{"id":"p9s3","text":"every evidence file to the subject and revision;
- value-hash assertions, so expected or observed va"},{"id":"p9s4","text":"lues never enter the audit index."},{"id":"p10s1","text":"Verification fails closed for missing, stale or invalid JSON evidence, subject/revision mismatch, fa"},{"id":"p10s2","text":"iled assertions, disallowed types, insufficient evidence or insufficient independent producers. The "},{"id":"p10s3","text":"output contains IDs, types, producers, paths into JSON, hashes, statuses, coverage and a determinist"},{"id":"p10s4","text":"ic SHA-256 pair-tree Merkle root. It never copies evidence bodies or assertion values."},{"id":"p11s1","text":"Files must be workspace-relative regular files. Symlinks, path escape, oversized input and excessive"},{"id":"p11s2","text":" structure are rejected. The plugin performs no network calls or child processes and writes only a c"},{"id":"p11s3","text":"ontent-addressed JSON index under the explicit `artifactDir`, followed by read-back verification."},{"id":"p12s1","text":"## CLI"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"The CLI emits one JSON object. A failed audit verdict exits `2`; invalid usage exits `1`."},{"id":"p15s1","text":"## DeepSeek Harness and MCP"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"The DSH bundle registers `dsh_audit_bundle_inspect` and `dsh_audit_bundle_verify`. These workspace-b"},{"id":"p16s2","text":"ounded tools dereference pinned evidence and can write the content-addressed index. The companion st"},{"id":"p16s3","text":"dio MCP server registers `audit_bundle_inspect` and `audit_bundle_verify` through `.mcp.json`, but a"},{"id":"p16s4","text":"ccepts only an inline manifest and structural JSONL receipts containing IDs, hashes, producer/subjec"},{"id":"p16s5","text":"t bindings and assertion digests. MCP never reads files, dereferences evidence, executes actions or "},{"id":"p16s6","text":"writes artifacts; it reports `evidenceContentVerification: not-performed`. Use DSH or CLI for real e"},{"id":"p16s7","text":"vidence-content verification."},{"id":"p17s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"## Verification"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"CI runs on Ubuntu and Windows. Node.js 22 or newer. MIT licensed."}],"truncated":false}
